===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)peys-}}
From {{suffix|en|spright|ly|pos2={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|adjective}}s with the sense ‘behaving like, having the nature of’|id2=adjectival}}.<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=adv.'', ''adj.'', and ''n|id=187717|date=March 2019|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref> {{m|en|spright|Spright}} is an obsolete variant of {{m|en|sprite|t=a shade, spirit; elf, fairy, goblin; apparition, ghost}}, from {{inh|en|enm|sprit|t=principle of life; soul, especially at the point of death; immaterial being (angel, demon, apparition, ghost, etc.); divine inspiration; Holy Spirit; the mind, intellect, reason; mental faculties, senses; power of prophecy; character, disposition; courage, resolution; mood, state of mind; human will; breath; (''alchemy'') volatile substance}}{{nb...|spreit, spreite, spret, sprete, spright, sprite, spriʒt|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=sprī̆t|pos=n|id=MED42433}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|esprite}}, {{m|xno|esprit}} and {{der|en|frm|esprit}}, variants of {{der|en|xno|-}}, {{der|en|frm|-}}, {{der|en|fro|espirit}}, {{m|fro|esperit|t=spirit}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=sprite|pos=n|id=187812|date=March 2019|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|entry=sprite|pos=n}}</ref> from {{der|en|la|spīritus|t=air; breath; breathing; ghost, spirit}}, from {{m|la|spīrō|t=to breathe; to breathe out, exhale}} (from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)peys-|t=to blow; to breathe}}) + {{m|la|-tus|t=suffix forming {{glossary|verbal noun}}s from {{glossary|verb}}s}}.

